{"schema":3,"source_digest":"c4365f050a4a82348716f23903d04f1371458bc659b662628ad329dbc8797a2e","dependencies":[],"processor_digest":"0e7e287f498782225c86635c4b16151adcc5552dc8a023621b89169c269e3a64","result":{"html":"<html><head></head><body><h2 id=\"from-source\">From source</h2>\n<p>Build <code>sessiond</code>, <code>sessionctl</code>, and the PAM module in release mode:</p>\n<html><head></head><body><pre class=\"highlight\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">cargo</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">build</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-p</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">sessiond</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-p</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">sessionctl</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-p</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">pam</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">--release</span><br></code></pre></body></html>\n<p>Install the binaries and PAM module:</p>\n<html><head></head><body><pre class=\"highlight\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">install</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-Dm755</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">target/release/sessiond</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">/usr/local/bin/sessiond</span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">install</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-Dm755</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">target/release/sessionctl</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">/usr/local/bin/sessionctl</span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">install</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-Dm755</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">target/release/libpam.so</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">/usr/lib/security/pam_sessiond.so</span><br></code></pre></body></html>\n<p>The <code>consolekit</code> feature enables the ConsoleKit compatibility layer. Include it\nwhen building if you need that support:</p>\n<html><head></head><body><pre class=\"highlight\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">cargo</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">build</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-p</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">sessiond</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">--release</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">--features</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">consolekit</span><br></code></pre></body></html>\n</body></html>","headers":[{"text":"From source","level":2,"id":"from-source"}],"title":null,"included_files":[]},"frontmatter":null}